+# ClinRef AI Integration — Implementation Plan
+
+## Summary
+
+Integrate Koog-based AI assistant into the existing ClinRef UpToDate Viewer app. The agent uses `MedicalDatabaseTools` (already built) to search/retrieve clinical content, streams responses through a SafetyValidator gate, and persists conversations via Room.
+
+---
+
+## Architecture Overview
+
+```
+domain/ai/           — Provider abstraction, agent factory, safety validation, streaming
+domain/chat/         — Conversation and message domain models
+data/local/          — Room DB, DAOs, entities, migrations
+data/secure/         — EncryptedSharedPreferences wrapper for API keys
+di/                  — Hilt modules (AiModule, DatabaseModule, SecurityModule)
+ui/chat/             — ChatScreen, ChatViewModel, composable components
+ui/settings/         — AiSettingsScreen, SettingsViewModel
+ui/conversations/    — ConversationListScreen
+```
+
+---
+
+## Phase 1: Gradle Dependencies & Room Setup
+
+### Files to modify
+- `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
+- `app/build.gradle.kts`
+
+### New dependencies (libs.versions.toml)
+```toml
+[versions]
+koog = "1.0.0"
+room = "2.7.1"
+securityCrypto = "1.1.0-alpha06"
+richtext = "0.5.1"
+
+[libraries]
+# Koog
+koog-agents = { group = "ai.koog", name = "koog-agents", version.ref = "koog" }
+koog-agents-additions = { group = "ai.koog", name = "koog-agents-additions", version.ref = "koog" }
+
+# Room
+room-runtime = { group = "androidx.room", name = "room-runtime", version.ref = "room" }
+room-ktx = { group = "androidx.room", name = "room-ktx", version.ref = "room" }
+room-compiler = { group = "androidx.room", name = "room-compiler", version.ref = "room" }
+
+# Security
+security-crypto = { group = "androidx.security", name = "security-crypto", version.ref = "securityCrypto" }
+
+# Markdown in Compose
+richtext-commonmark = { group = "com.mikepenz", name = "richtext-commonmark", version.ref = "richtext" }
+richtext-material3 = { group = "com.mikepenz", name = "richtext-material3", version.ref = "richtext" }
+```
+
+### app/build.gradle.kts additions
+```kotlin
+implementation(libs.koog.agents)
+implementation(libs.koog.agents.additions)
+implementation(libs.room.runtime)
+implementation(libs.room.ktx)
+ksp(libs.room.compiler)
+implementation(libs.security.crypto)
+implementation(libs.richtext.commonmark)
+implementation(libs.richtext.material3)
+```
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2: AI Configuration Domain
+
+### New file: `domain/ai/AiProvider.kt`
+```kotlin
+enum class AiProvider(val displayName: String) {
+    OPENAI("OpenAI"),
+    ANTHROPIC("Anthropic"),
+    GOOGLE("Google"),
+    DEEPSEEK("DeepSeek"),
+    OPENROUTER("OpenRouter"),
+    OLLAMA("Ollama (Local)")
+}
+```
+
+### New file: `domain/ai/AiConfiguration.kt`
+```kotlin
+@Serializable
+data class AiConfiguration(
+    val provider: AiProvider = AiProvider.OPENAI,
+    val baseUrl: String = "",
+    val model: String = "",
+    val temperature: Float = 0.3f,
+    val maxTokens: Int = 4096,
+    val historyCompressionThreshold: Int = 8000,
+    val isConfigured: Boolean = false
+)
+```
+Note: `apiKey` is deliberately excluded from `AiConfiguration` serialization. It is stored and retrieved separately via `SecurePreferences.getApiKey(provider)`. This prevents accidental serialization of the key into JSON logs, conversation history, or any DataStore/SharedPreferences backup.
+
+### New file: `domain/ai/PatientProfile.kt`
+```kotlin
+@Serializable
+data class PatientProfile(
+    val age: String = "",
+    val sex: String = "",
+    val conditions: List<String> = emptyList(),
+    val medications: List<String> = emptyList(),
+    val allergies: List<String> = emptyList(),
+    val notes: String = ""
+) {
+    fun toSystemBlock(): String { /* format for system prompt */ }
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## Phase 3: Encrypted API Key Storage
+
+### New file: `data/secure/SecurePreferences.kt`
+
+Uses `EncryptedSharedPreferences` with `MasterKey.KeyScheme.AES256_GCM`:
+- `saveApiKey(provider, key)` / `getApiKey(provider)`
+- `saveConfiguration(config)` / `loadConfiguration()`
+- Exposes `StateFlow<AiConfiguration>` for reactive settings observation
+
+---
+
+## Phase 4: Room Database for Conversations
+
+### Build Setup
+
+Room 2.8.4 supports KMP. The `@ConstructedBy` pattern with `expect/actual` is required even for Android-only projects.
+
+**`libs.versions.toml`**:
+```toml
+[versions]
+room = "2.8.4"
+sqlite = "2.7.0"
+
+[libraries]
+room-runtime = { module = "androidx.room:room-runtime", version.ref = "room" }
+room-compiler = { module = "androidx.room:room-compiler", version.ref = "room" }
+sqlite-bundled = { module = "androidx.sqlite:sqlite-bundled", version.ref = "sqlite" }
+
+[plugins]
+androidx-room = { id = "androidx.room", version.ref = "room" }
+```
+
+**Root `build.gradle.kts`**:
+```kotlin
+plugins {
+    alias(libs.plugins.androidx.room) apply false
+}
+```
+
+**App `build.gradle.kts`**:
+```kotlin
+plugins {
+    alias(libs.plugins.androidx.room)
+}
+
+room {
+    schemaDirectory("$projectDir/schemas")
+}
+
+dependencies {
+    implementation(libs.room.runtime)
+    implementation(libs.sqlite.bundled)
+    ksp(libs.room.compiler)
+}
+```
+
+### New file: `data/local/AppDatabase.kt`
+```kotlin
+@Database(
+    entities = [ConversationEntity::class, MessageEntity::class],
+    version = 1,
+    exportSchema = true
+)
+@TypeConverters(Converters::class)
+@ConstructedBy(AppDatabaseConstructor::class)
+abstract class AppDatabase : RoomDatabase() {
+    abstract fun conversationDao(): ConversationDao
+    abstract fun messageDao(): MessageDao
+}
+
+@Suppress("KotlinNoActualForExpect")
+expect object AppDatabaseConstructor : RoomDatabaseConstructor<AppDatabase> {
+    override fun initialize(): AppDatabase
+}
+```
+
+**Android actual** (`androidMain` or same source set for Android-only):
+```kotlin
+actual object AppDatabaseConstructor : RoomDatabaseConstructor<AppDatabase> {
+    override fun initialize(): AppDatabase = createRoomDatabase()
+}
+
+private fun createRoomDatabase(): AppDatabase {
+    val context = /* get from Hilt or injected */
+    val dbFile = context.getDatabasePath("clinref_ai.db")
+    return Room.databaseBuilder<AppDatabase>(
+        context = context,
+        name = dbFile.absolutePath
+    )
+    .fallbackToDestructiveMigration()
+    .build()
+}
+```
+
+Note: For an Android-only project without KMP source sets, the `expect/actual` can live in the same `main` source set. Room's KSP processor handles the generation.
+
+### New file: `data/local/entity/ConversationEntity.kt`
+```kotlin
+@Entity(tableName = "conversations")
+data class ConversationEntity(
+    @PrimaryKey val id: String,
+    val title: String,
+    val patientProfile: String,      // JSON
+    val createdAt: Long,             // UTC epoch millis
+    val updatedAt: Long,             // UTC epoch millis
+    val promptTokens: Int = 0,
+    val completionTokens: Int = 0,
+    val toolTokens: Int = 0,
+    val tokenLimit: Int = 100_000
+) {
+    val totalTokens: Int get() = promptTokens + completionTokens + toolTokens
+}
+```
+
+### New file: `data/local/entity/MessageEntity.kt`
+```kotlin
+@Entity(
+    tableName = "messages",
+    foreignKeys = [ForeignKey(
+        entity = ConversationEntity::class,
+        parentColumns = ["id"],
+        childColumns = ["conversationId"],
+        onDelete = ForeignKey.CASCADE
+    )],
+    indices = [Index("conversationId")]
+)
+data class MessageEntity(
+    @PrimaryKey val id: String,
+    val conversationId: String,
+    val role: String,           // "user", "assistant", "system", "cancelled"
+    val content: String,
+    val timestamp: Long,        // UTC epoch millis — always System.currentTimeMillis()
+    val toolCallsJson: String? = null,
+    val citationsJson: String? = null,
+    val warningsJson: String? = null
+)
+```
+The `"cancelled"` role persists a partial-generation message for auditability when the user hits cancel mid-generation.
+
+### DAOs
+Standard Room DAOs with reactive `Flow<List<>>` queries. Already compatible with Room 2.8.4 KMP (suspend + Flow).
+
+### DI: `di/DatabaseModule.kt`
+```kotlin
+@Module
+@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)
+object DatabaseModule {
+    @Provides @Singleton
+    fun provideDatabase(@ApplicationContext context: Context): AppDatabase {
+        val dbFile = context.getDatabasePath("clinref_ai.db")
+        return Room.databaseBuilder<AppDatabase>(
+            context = context,
+            name = dbFile.absolutePath
+        )
+        .fallbackToDestructiveMigration()
+        .build()
+    }
+
+    @Provides fun provideConversationDao(db: AppDatabase) = db.conversationDao()
+    @Provides fun provideMessageDao(db: AppDatabase) = db.messageDao()
+}
+```
+Note: Room 2.8.4 KMP automatically uses the bundled SQLite driver on Android. No explicit `setDriver()` needed for Android-only projects.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 5: SafetyValidator
+
+### New file: `domain/ai/SafetyValidator.kt`
+
+Provider-independent structural validator. Six rules:
+
+```kotlin
+class SafetyValidator {
+
+    data class ValidationResult(
+        val passed: Boolean,
+        val warnings: List<String>,
+        val blockedReason: String? = null
+    )
+
+    data class TurnContext(
+        val toolCalls: List<ToolCallRecord>,
+        val answer: String,
+        val citations: List<Citation>,
+        val sectionWarnings: Map<String, Boolean> = emptyMap(),
+        val toolResults: List<String> = emptyList(),  // raw text returned by each tool call
+        val fetchedSections: List<FetchedSection> = emptyList()  // metadata of sections actually fetched
+    )
+
+    data class FetchedSection(
+        val topicId: String,
+        val topicTitle: String,
+        val sectionId: String,
+        val sectionTitle: String
+    )
+
+    fun validate(context: TurnContext): ValidationResult
+}
+```
+
+**Rule 1 — Tool call required**: Reject if `turnToolCalls` is empty (no successful tool call in this turn).
+
+**Rule 1b — Section content required**: At least one successful `getTopicSectionText()` call must have occurred. Reject if the turn only contains `searchTopics` and/or `getTopicOutline` calls but no `getTopicSectionText` call. This prevents answers based on titles/outlines alone — the answer must be grounded in actual section content.
+
+**Rule 2 — Citation-to-tool consistency**: For every citation in the final answer, verify that:
+- The cited `topicTitle` was retrieved in the current turn (exists in `fetchedSections`)
+- The cited `sectionId` was retrieved in the current turn (exists in `fetchedSections`)
+- The cited `sectionTitle` matches the retrieved section metadata (fuzzy match: `contains` or `equalsIgnoreCase`)
+
+If any citation references content that was not actually fetched, block with "Citation references section not retrieved in this turn." This directly checks grounding instead of using a heuristic similarity score.
+
+**Rule 3 — Complex data warning**: Flag any answer referencing a section with `sectionWarnings[sectionId] == true` unless the answer contains the warning text.
+
+**Rule 4 — No invented numbers (verbatim match)**: Every numeric token in the final answer (regex: `\d+[\.,]?\d*\s*(mg|%|mL|mmol|mcg|units?|mEq|L|kg|cm|mmHg)?`) must appear verbatim (or near-verbatim with unit normalization) in at least one of the `toolResults` from this turn. If any numeric token in the answer cannot be found in tool output, block with "Answer contains numbers not traceable to retrieved source data." This directly enforces "no invented numbers" without punishing legitimate multi-topic comparisons where each fact comes from its own source.
+
+**Rule 5 — Citation required**: Require at least one citation containing exact `topicTitle`, `sectionTitle`, and `sectionId` retrieved during the current turn.
+
+### Tests: `app/src/test/java/com/clinref/app/domain/ai/SafetyValidatorTest.kt`
+- Each rule tested independently with positive/negative cases
+- Rule 1b: test "searchTopics + getTopicOutline only, no getTopicSectionText" blocks; test "getTopicSectionText present" passes
+- Rule 2: test "citation matches fetched section" passes; test "citation references unfetched section" blocks; test "fuzzy sectionTitle match" passes
+- Rule 4: test "two independent facts from two sources" passes (each number traceable); test "invented number not in any tool result" blocks
+- Combined validation tested
+- Edge cases: empty answer, no tools, single citation, multiple citations, cancelled generation
+
